reviews\n\nSina Mousavi\n\n28 reviews 35 followers\n\nFollow\n\nFollow\n\nJune 6, 2020\n\nThe Economics of the Second World War: Seventy-Five Years On is a collection of short articles that examines the interrelations between economics and the causes, the conduct, and the consequences of World War 2 throughout the globe. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n100 Years of Plastic: Using the Past to Guide the Future by Chao Liu, Roland Geyer, Shanying Hu :: SSRN (https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=6550384)\nciteturn14search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Crawled: last month; \n\n# 100 Years of Plastic: Using the Past to Guide the Future\n\n22 Pages Posted: 9 Apr 2026\n\nSee all articles by Chao Liu\n\n## Chao Liu\n\nTsinghua University\n\n## Roland Geyer\n\nUniversity of California, Santa Barbara (UCSB) - Donald Bren School of Environmental Science & Management\n\n## Shanying Hu\n\nTsinghua University\n\n### Abstract\n\nRobust and credible historical material flow data are necessary to support the ongoing efforts to reconcile the economic and social benefits of plastics with their human and environmental health impacts. This study presents material flow analysis (MFA) for all plastic polymers and applications at all life cycle stages for the period 1950-2020 across the world which is separated into China, Europe, North America (NA) and the rest of the world. 3 scenarios for the next 30 years were projected. Historical account shows that, over the past 70 years, about 1.9 billion metric tons plastic waste was mismanaged, where China, Europe and NA contributed about 10%, 11% and 8%, respectively. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n100+ Years of Plastics. Leo Baekeland and Beyond 9780841226777, 9780841226784 - DOKUMEN.PUB (https://dokumen.pub/100-years-of-plastics-leo-baekeland-and-beyond-9780841226777-9780841226784.html)\nciteturn14search4 [wordlim